  "description": [
    {
      "value": "<p>What is left of a body that lost its mantle, either to a giant impact or to the star, depending on which model is currently in fashion. It is four tenths of an Earth radius of nickel-iron under a skin of silicate breccia, locked to Tenter at eleven and a half days, with a sunward face at 214 degrees and a night face four hundred degrees colder. Surface gravity is twice Earth&#39;s, which makes it the most uncomfortable body in the sector to work on. Nothing lives on it or in it.</p>",
      "inLanguage": [{ "id": ["core.peerdb.org", "LANGUAGE", "en-GB"] }]
    }
  ],
